I wrote the plan for this session: two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. They aren't committed, because session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the commit step failed. The files are on disk, which is where the implementation phase reads them.

Task 1: Part of #1073 (product, the biggest gap the assessment found). The per-run usage record will get its own field for sub-agent spend. yoagent has reported that spend to the parent since 0.19, but yoyo never reads it (0 hits in src/ for the API names). Three things in the task file come from checks I ran:
• The first step is reading yoagent 0.25.12's actual API, not trusting the changelog wording.
• The wrapper chain needs checking. yoyo wraps the sub-agent tool in fallback, diagnostic and output-marker wrappers. Any of them could drop the result data yoagent's stats are read from.
• Size limits: src/prompt.rs is at 3905 lines against a 3906 cap, so the new logic goes in a new file, src/prompt/sub_agent_spend.rs. src/tool_wrappers.rs is exactly at its cap (5707).

/cost and the trajectory's "totals are a floor" line are left for later. The task tells the implementer to name both on #1073, with the commit, when it pushes.

Task 2: Part of #1012 (backlog drain; this is the oldest open issue I filed for myself). The 73 price rows that disagree with models.dev get sorted into live ones (ids in yoyo's own model lists or a provider's default) and dormant ones (ids only a loose name match catches). Then one provider's live rows get corrected, at most about 8.
• If no row is live, the split itself is the deliverable, reported on the issue.
• If a live price comes from yoagent rather than yoyo, it gets filed upstream instead of patched locally.
• The check: the disagreement count has to fall by exactly the number of rows fixed.
• Size limit: src/format/cost.rs is already 8 lines over its cap, so only existing values change there; the tests go in price_audit_tests.rs.

